---
import WikiLayout from '../../layouts/WikiLayout.astro';
import { localizedAlternates } from '../../i18n/utils';
import { coreSeoKeywords } from '../../i18n/seo-keywords';
const seoKeywords = coreSeoKeywords('en', 'tools');
const tools=[{name:'Loadout Builder',url:'/tools/loadout-builder/',text:'Plan a role-focused kit and follow the relevant database links.'},{name:'Weapon Compare',url:'/tools/weapon-compare/',text:'Compare two weapon references side by side.'},{name:'Vehicle Compare',url:'/tools/vehicle-compare/',text:'Compare battlefield roles across vehicle entries.'}];
---
<WikiLayout title="WARDOGS Tools" description="Interactive WARDOGS tools for loadout planning and weapon or vehicle comparison." canonicalPath="/tools/" pageType="CollectionPage" schemaItems={tools} primaryKeyword={seoKeywords[0]} keywords={seoKeywords.slice(1)} image="/images/entities/entity-comparison-workbench.jpg" imageAlt="WARDOGS tactical planning workbench for comparing entities and loadouts" imageWidth={2172} imageHeight={724} alternates={localizedAlternates('tools')} xDefaultPath="/tools/" showAd={true} adPlacement="tool">
  <p class="eyebrow">INTERACTIVE KNOWLEDGE TOOLS</p><h1>WARDOGS Tools</h1><p>Use these lightweight tools to choose a starting point, then open the connected Wiki entries for evidence, context and patch-bound details. They organize decisions; they do not invent stats or replace the underlying database.</p>
  <figure class="knowledge-hero-media"><img src="/images/entities/entity-comparison-workbench.jpg" alt="Illustrated tactical planning workbench for comparing WARDOGS entities and loadouts" width="2172" height="724" loading="lazy" decoding="async" fetchpriority="low" /><figcaption>Comparison tools connect choices to version-bound entity records and guides.</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="database-hub-grid">{tools.map((tool)=><a href={tool.url}><strong>{tool.name}</strong><small>{tool.text}</small></a>)}</div>
  <section><h2>How to use these tools</h2><p>Begin with the decision you need to make. Use Loadout Builder when the question is about a complete role and budget. Use Weapon Compare for two combat options, or Vehicle Compare when transport and crew purpose matter. After making a selection, follow the database links to confirm what is known for the current patch.</p><h2>Data boundaries</h2><p>Tool output is descriptive rather than a hidden-stat calculator. When a price, damage value, speed or armor figure cannot be supported, its status is <strong>Currently unconfirmed</strong>. This prevents a convenient interface from giving uncertain data more authority than its sources justify.</p></section>
  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do tools save my choices?</h3><p>No. Current tools run locally in the browser and do not create an account or store a permanent build.</p><h3>Are tool recommendations official?</h3><p>No. They are Wiki navigation aids. Entity records and cited guides provide the supporting context.</p></section>
</WikiLayout>
